    - Kana: "\u306F"
      Kanji: 
      Key: "\u306F"
      Explanation: "\u306F (pronounced \u308F) is often considered to be one of the
        most difficult particles to master in Japanese. \u306F marks the topic of
        the sentence, and describes the whole sentence broadly."
      Examples:
      - Question: "\u79C1___\u30C8\u30E0\u3067\u3059\u3002"
